From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@y>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 13:08:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lavu/hwcontext_v4l2request: tag NV15 and NV20 as themselves

V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV15 and NV20 are packed: four 10-bit samples in five bytes,
no padding. The table gave them the planar logical sw_format YUV420P10 and
YUV422P10, which describes neither the plane count nor the sample layout of
the buffer the decoder writes.

Because the tag was wrong, everything generic that would act on it had to
be switched off. transfer_get_formats() blanks its whole format list when
sw_format is YUV420P, YUV420P10 or YUV422P10, and map_from() returns ENOSYS
for the same three -- so hwdownload of a 10-bit frame fails for every target
format, not just for one, and hwmap fails outright. On RK3588 that is every
10-bit HEVC, VP9 and AV1 frame the stateless decoder produces, and it is why
HDR content has to fall back to software decode to reach a tone mapper.

AV_PIX_FMT_NV15 and AV_PIX_FMT_NV20 describe the buffer exactly, and
swscale reads both, so tag them honestly and the machinery works as it
stands: hwdownload yields a real NV15 frame, hwmap maps the dma-buf with no
copy, and `format=yuv420p10le` unpacks. map_frame() needs nothing -- it
fills data[] and linesize[] from the DRM layer descriptors and never
consults sw_format.

The two guards are left alone on purpose. They still name the planar tags,
which is still correct for the entries that genuinely carry one: the
Allwinner tiled NV12, the Broadcom SAND128 pair, and the AFBC formats all
keep a logical tag that does not match their layout, and none of them may be
downloaded or mapped.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
index b6633d9..f08f981 100644
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_v4l2request.c
@@ -70,11 +70,11 @@ static const struct {
     { V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_32L32, AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P, DRM_FORMAT_NV12, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_ALLWINNER_TILED, 8 },
 #endif
 #if defined(V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV15) && defined(DRM_FORMAT_NV15)
-    { V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV15, AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P10, DRM_FORMAT_NV15, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR, 10 },
+    { V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV15, AV_PIX_FMT_NV15, DRM_FORMAT_NV15, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR, 10 },
 #endif
     { V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV16, AV_PIX_FMT_NV16, DRM_FORMAT_NV16, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR, 8 },
 #if defined(V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV20) && defined(DRM_FORMAT_NV20)
-    { V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV20, AV_PIX_FMT_YUV422P10, DRM_FORMAT_NV20, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR, 10 },
+    { V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV20, AV_PIX_FMT_NV20, DRM_FORMAT_NV20, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR, 10 },
 #endif
 #if defined(V4L2_PIX_FMT_P010) && defined(DRM_FORMAT_P010)
     { V4L2_PIX_FMT_P010, AV_PIX_FMT_P010, DRM_FORMAT_P010, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR, 10 },
